# Task 2: `/dtwin/metrics/history` spans versions

## Context

Continuing the Task 1 work above: the analytics run-history endpoint backing
Knowledge Graph → Management → Runs (a page with no version filter) used to
hard-scope its read to `domain.current_version`, so a domain whose current
version happened to be blank showed an empty history even with rows on file
for earlier versions. The endpoint now spans every version by default and
takes an optional `?version=` to scope back to one, matching the store
contract Task 1 widened.

## Changes

1. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py` — `GET /metrics/history` rewritten:
   added `Query` to the `fastapi` import; the handler now takes
   `version: Optional[str] = Query(default=None)` and
   `limit: int = Query(default=200, ge=1, le=1000)` (default rises from 100
   to 200 to match `/domain/build-runs` — the write cap stays 100 per
   `(domain, version)`, so spanning N versions can yield up to
   `min(limit, 100 × N)` rows and `limit` is now the real bound); the guard
   dropped `or not version` (guarding on version reported an empty history
   whenever `current_version` was blank) and now checks `folder` only; the
   registry call forwards the query `version` (not `domain.current_version`)
   and the query `limit`.
2. `tests/units/dtwin/test_metrics_history.py` (new) — Investigated whether
   this could be a behavioural test instead of the brief's source-text
   assertions (its own caveat: exercising the endpoint needs a session with
   a loaded domain plus a configured registry). Found the existing `client`
   fixture (`TestClient(shared.fastapi.main.app)`) already drives internal
   `/dtwin/*` routes with no domain loaded in `tests/units/api/test_routes.py`
   (`test_neighbors_with_uri_no_domain`), and `get_domain` /
   `RegistryService.from_context` are the only two seams that need a domain
   (both plain module-level names, patchable without touching the endpoint's
   own control flow). Wrote a real behavioural suite driving
   `GET /dtwin/metrics/history` through the FastAPI test client instead of
   reading source text: a no-domain-loaded smoke test needs no mocking at
   all; the domain-loaded cases patch `api.routers.internal.dtwin.get_domain`
   (returns a tiny `_FakeDomain` with `uc_domain_folder` set and
   `current_version=""`) and
   `back.objects.registry.RegistryService.RegistryService.from_context`
   (returns a `_FakeRegistryService` recording each call, mirroring the
   brief's `_FakeService`). Covers: omitting `version` forwards `None` to the
   registry even when `current_version` is blank (the regression this task
   fixes); an explicit `?version=` is still forwarded; the default `limit` is
   200 and an explicit `?limit=` is forwarded; `limit` outside `[1, 1000]`
   is rejected with 422. No source-text assertions were needed or kept.

