# Feature summary: analytics run history moves to the Runs page

Closing summary of the whole `feat/graph-analytics-lakeflow-pushdown` Runs-
page feature (Tasks 1-7 above), for anyone scanning this log later without
reading every task section.

**Before:** analytics run history lived behind the eighth tab of Knowledge
Graph → Analytics, scoped to the domain's *current* version only (empty if
that version happened to be blank), read via `GET /dtwin/metrics/history`
with a mandatory `version`.

**After:** analytics run history lives on Knowledge Graph → Management →
Runs, as a second table stacked below the pre-existing build-runs table
(they share no columns, so they stay separate rather than merging). Both
tables always show every version, newest first — the page's old
`runsVersionFilter` dropdown (which only ever scoped the build table) is
gone rather than kept and widened, since a filter governing one table and
not the other would be worse than none. `GET /dtwin/metrics/history` now
takes an optional `version` (omitted = every version) and an optional
`limit` (default 200, max 1000, up from a fixed 100). A failed analytics run
renders a red "Failed" badge with dashed-out metric cells instead of the
zeros the store recorded internally. A Details button opens a modal with
the full scope (local names + raw URIs), graph metrics, duration, task ID
and any error text. The two tables fetch and render independently, so one
endpoint failing never blanks the other. The Analytics page's History tab
is gone with no in-app pointer to its replacement (Task 5); the equivalent
dead Runs section on the Domain page is gone too, since that page's menu
never declared a `runs` item and could never reach it (Task 6). This log's
Task 7 documents both changes in `docs/user-guide.md`.

