# Final whole-branch review: six findings fixed

## Context

A final whole-branch review of the completed Runs-page feature (Tasks 1-7
above) returned six findings: two must-fix, four recommended. All six are
small and independent; fixed together in one pass.

## Changes

1. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-runs.js` (**must-fix**) —
   `_loadBuildRuns()` and `_loadAnalyticsRuns()` now return `true` on a
   successful load (including a genuinely empty result — an empty domain is
   not a load failure) and `false` from both their `!data.success` branch
   and their `catch` block. `loadDomainRuns()` sets `_runsLoaded = buildOk
   && analyticsOk` instead of latching `true` unconditionally, so a load
   that errored is retried on the next `sidebarSectionChanged` re-entry
   instead of re-showing a stale error forever. Each loader keeps its own
   `try` block and its own error element — no `Promise.all`/`allSettled`
   introduced, isolation stays structural. An empty-but-successful load
   still latches: "no runs yet" is a real, current answer for that section
   visit, not a failure that should be retried on every single re-entry
   (the reviewer flagged the pre-split code's opposite bug — never
   latching on empty — for exactly this reason).
2. `docs/user-guide.md` (**must-fix**) — Line 585 no longer claims the
   entity-type filter is "pushed down to the graph store" or that it works
   around an "in-memory limit" — both false since the NetworkX/pushdown
   compute paths were deleted (commit b91b1cf) and contradicted line 567 of
   the same section. Now says the filter is applied in SQL inside the
   Lakeflow job against the Delta snapshot, and that there is no in-memory
   limit to work around.
3. `src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py`, `DigitalTwin.py`
   (**recommended**) — Two stale comments referencing the deleted Analytics
   "History" tab now point to the analytics table on the Runs page
   (Knowledge Graph → Management → Runs), where this data actually
   surfaces. Comments only, no logic changed.
4. `tests/units/front/test_runs_page.py` (**recommended**) —
   `test_failed_analytics_rows_do_not_show_zeroed_metrics` used to assert
   only `"_analyticsRunRow" in _js()`, which would pass against a renderer
   that printed the stored zeros — the exact bug the name claims to guard.
   Rewritten to extract the function body and assert each numeric metric
   column is gated `failed ? dash : ...` rather than calling the raw
   formatter unconditionally.
5. `tests/units/front/test_runs_page.py` (**recommended**) —
   `test_the_two_fetches_are_independent`'s `"Promise.all" not in src` was
   a substring check that also forbade `Promise.allSettled` — the one
   combinator that would make loader isolation structural. Changed to
   `"Promise.all(" not in src` and reworded the docstring.
6. `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py` (**recommended**) —
   `test_no_dead_runs_section`'s function-local `from pathlib import Path`
   moved to the module-level imports, matching the rest of the file.

Also added `test_runs_loaded_flag_is_not_latched_unconditionally` and
